Then, he won 6 more tickets. So, I need to add those 6 tickets to the 24 he had left. Let me add 24 and 6. 24 plus 6 is 30. So, after winning the additional 6 tickets, he should have 30 tickets in total. 

Wait, let me check my steps again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Starting with 49, subtracting 25 gives 24. Then adding 6 gives 30. Yeah, that seems right. Alternatively, I could have thought of it as 49 minus 25 is 24, then 24 plus 6 is 30. Both ways, the result is the same. 

Is there another way to approach this? Maybe combining the operations. So, total tickets = initial tickets - spent tickets + won tickets. That would be 49 - 25 + 6. Calculating that, 49 - 25 is 24, then 24 + 6 is 30. Yep, same answer. 

